[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43609\">#43609</a>, I tried to make <code>ChainComplex.of</code> implicit reducible def, but it turns out having some problems in removinging usages of  <code>ChainComplex.of_X</code>. Here is an example of what happens multiple times.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Homology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HomologicalComplex</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasZeroMorphisms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddRightCancelSemigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">One</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eqToHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">Ne</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d_comp_d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hjk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">subst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hjk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">eqToHom_refl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id_comp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dite_eq_ite</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ite_true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"o\">]}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of'_X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasZeroMorphisms</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of'_X</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of'_X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 623105088,
        "sender_full_name": "Nailin Guan",
        "timestamp": 1789036192
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What problem do you see here? The example succeeds in Lean 4 Web, and it even succeeds if I remove the <code>ChainComplex.of_X</code> mention. Which Lean version are you using?</p>\n<p>I'd also be interested in understanding what made you consider making it implicit-reducible. Perhaps we can find a better solution to your problem (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XY_problem\">#xy</a>).</p>",
        "id": 623106969,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1789036719
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem is on removing <code>ChainComplex.of_X</code>, then simp won't work.<br>\nI am on <code>leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2</code>, a commit of mathlib 2 days ago.<br>\nIt is <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"699016\">@Edison Xie</span> 's suggestions, but sorry I haven't got a complete understanding of this.</p>",
        "id": 623107848,
        "sender_full_name": "Nailin Guan",
        "timestamp": 1789036974
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm sorry, I think I haven't understood what concrete example fails. The one above doesn't seem to fail on 4.34-rc2. Could you please provide an example that actually shows an error or other unexpected behavior?</p>",
        "id": 623108520,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1789037125
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe it was a <code>def</code> until <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"699016\">@Edison Xie</span> made it an <code>abbrev</code> recently. Indeed, it would probably be a slightly better design (and more coherent with recent modifications we have made in order to remove some <code>set_option</code>) to make it an <code>implicit_reducible</code> def (but with the <code>simps X</code> attribute).</p>",
        "id": 623108576,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1789037145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm just wondering about the motivations to make it implicit-reducible. Is there a <code>Functor.comp</code>-like use case here?</p>",
        "id": 623108732,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1789037205
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note: this is probably a specific <code>mathlib</code> topic/issue. There is no evidence that there is anything wrong with Lean here :-)</p>",
        "id": 623108797,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1789037225
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is indeed failing on commit <code>98b840b</code>.<br>\nAnyway, this seems to be fixed by actions in mathlib, I'll investigate</p>",
        "id": 623109229,
        "sender_full_name": "Nailin Guan",
        "timestamp": 1789037364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459699\">Joël Riou</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/A.20hint.20on.20possible.20problem.20in.20.40.5Bimplicit_reducible.5D/near/623108797\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note: this is probably a specific <code>mathlib</code> topic/issue. There is no evidence that there is anything wrong with Lean here :-)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That might be true. I'm just hoping to learn if there are any other reasons for using <code>implicit_reducible</code> that I wasn't aware of yet. I've been trying to find alternative solutions to most of these use cases in the recent days, so it would still interest me what prompts this change</p>",
        "id": 623109293,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1789037384
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"221653\">Paul Reichert</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/A.20hint.20on.20possible.20problem.20in.20.40.5Bimplicit_reducible.5D/near/623108732\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm just wondering about the motivations to make it implicit-reducible. Is there a <code>Functor.comp</code>-like use case here?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Basically all the definitions of structures where an object of a category may appear in a field should be made <code>implicit_reducible</code> or an <code>abbrev</code> (so that <code>rw/simp</code> do not need <code>set_option</code>). In the library, we are using much more <code>implicit_reducible</code> defs rather than <code>abbrev</code>. Basically, in most cases, repurposing/specializing certains typeclasses is made by doing <code>abbrev</code> (e.g. <code>HasCoproduct</code> which is an abbrev for <code>HasLimit</code>), and definitions of a term belonging to a structure is usually made by <code>@[implicit_reducible, simps] def</code>. This is mostly a matter of consistency.</p>",
        "id": 623110294,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1789037698
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry, I am stupid here, I didn't correctly use <code>of'</code>, I updated the original one, for Lean4 Web, see <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=LYewJgrgNgpgUHADhARlAlgYwATuIkAJwBdsBZAQ2IAsMUA6AQSgHMYVCL6AJEUKECwCePPiAEssFKAGE%2BiWAA8EIRDAB22GVRgsiQgCrUY%2BhOorAYAZ0QVMMLdQrp1c%2FEoQA3CoXQU0DgDeAGrYAFzYBkJqAFQAvtgA2trEuvox2MEAukkAMnjoxFY8FFYAWjCEIGREiNToVsBWmVlw2NiBgI3A4ZHRMPFJjGBgAEroLNTE2ur2UADKMMDjVRCI2J05iQDy6g4bSQAiMJjoYP6wAKIAjuutcAACiXgKWIUA%2BoQwkCcBrWAwADNsCAAQBybAACgAGj1uoAkwkyAEpIWAeoAAImw6gANNgYRDNABqbAARmRgDfyXGY5EQqw3CIY7HYVH47BE0nYQDWREzMdgALzYAAMyLCbXajmcrnkSky63CvNFgUpYX5UNF7VR6GwACs5bggdQepr%2BTq2dgaBpsDArgYQLxgJCUEJsIQAO5JahZZFc1E6mBQKwOAVq7BWJxqXUAiCaTU6t28gB82EdIeeSQhADkYPQrEJgPaXYjWmKmW9MPI3mBwcrsJHo9rsABrbD1HXULVNhNJoTB9pWVBWUgt5vtnsp%2FDA9RQJ2JK02u0fQFQHEpNKEESnUvyHFgQowN5Wt67nG7t7EQgQGA42lZOIIWB5ijAsFvPEwiLwpEo9GYnF4wkk8lKXUalaW%2FRlmX%2FdlvR5fkhUhTV32FSEZCcFw3AUGBFHoEFwRhVFaURegYSNSkEPldpCABKAEH8DgYE8bAAC9KhASE31lBFgiQlCJXQ6VQm6ZVRR4tCpUw7CwUpCFa2wN5sEAMsJBWpGTNHk4N8iWIoSnKFiakIOoGiaehmKqTdx2hSFINZADkSFBBMIsDC2NhbBOKQkE7UhGTNUUwBWDcATf3nPQRFlKjHlFOTKxU2SVDJXccScJfT0%2BWwALIRM1ioWFflHVFTDiFFKLxxi3ixKwxKoTuDRUREuKMOUIA\">this</a>, commenting out the additional simp lemma would break it.</p>",
